<title>BELGIUM: EU says real estate sales can be used to meet EMU.</title>
<headline>EU says real estate sales can be used to meet EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eurostat, the EU's statistical office, said on Monday that governments wishing to qualify for economic and monetary union could sell real estate holdings to lower their budget deficits.</p>
<p>&quot;If a state wished to sell its property it would normally have an impact on its deficit,&quot; a Eurostat official told a news conference.</p>
<p>The statistical body made a distinction between the sales of financial assets, such as gold, and real assets in the effect on public sector deficits.</p>
<p>While gold sales can be applied towards a reduction in public sector debt outstanding, they cannot be used in reducing annual deficits.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 68730</p>
</text>
